; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   416   *********************************************************************************************************************/
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   417  /*!
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   418   * \brief Checks whether current redundant block can and shall be repaired or not.
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   419   * \details We decide between three situations:
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   420   *          1. both blocks are valid, nothing to repair
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   421   *          2. both blocks are defect, NvM cannot repair
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   422   *          3. only one block is defect, NvM will try to repair the redundancy
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   423   * \return FALSE block does not have to be repaired or cannot be repaired
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   424   * \return TRUE  block is defect and shall be repaired
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   425   * \context TASK
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   426   * \reentrant FALSE
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM_Qry.c	   427   * \synchronous TRUE
